From ac8d5a386968b23d5805f374de550cf051b493cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: b1air <dimazzzzz342@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:42:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add floating_snap and snap: floating windows to halves and
 quarters

`floating_snap <px>|off` snaps a floating window dragged to within that
many pixels of its output's left or right edge to that half of the
screen, near the top or bottom of the edge to a quarter, and to the top
edge to all of it; a preview, drawn as the tiling drop indicator is,
shows where while the cursor is there. Not the bottom edge: that is
where a dock is. Dragged away again, more than a few pixels so that a
click on the title bar leaves it be, the window gets its size back
under the cursor.

`snap left|right|top|bottom|top-left|top-right|bottom-left|
bottom-right|maximize|restore` does the same for the focused floating
window from a binding or over IPC, floating_snap on or off.

The zones are the output's usable area with the workspace's gaps round
them and between the halves, where tiled windows would be. A window
resized by hand, or tiled again, is no longer snapped. get_tree reports
the zone as "snapped".
